{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>By number, forty shall he strike him.</b> They flog him with two sets from behind him and one from before him (Makkot 23), for every sinner turns his back to the Shekhinah and makes as though the Eye above does not see. And there is a sinner who brazenly faces HaShem, as it says (Proverbs 21:29): ״הֵעֵז אִישׁ רָשָׁע בְּפָנָיו״. And just as the Torah was stricter with the thief than with the robber, and the double payment was imposed upon him because he denies the Eye above and does not acknowledge a servant before his master — unlike the robber (Bava Kamma 79:) — so too the double portion was imposed upon him to be flogged twofold from behind and one portion from before, for in every sin it is possible that he brazenly faced Him or that he turned his back to HaShem, and then his sin is doubled." "And some say: one from before him — for he should have remembered one thing from before him, for he came from a putrid drop; and two from behind him — for he should have remembered that he is going to a place of maggots, and remembered before whom he is destined to give judgment and account, and these are behind him. And this is correct." "And the reason for the number thirty-nine: because he denied the One that ascends to the number thirteen, and the Torah that is expounded by thirteen hermeneutical principles, and rebelled against the good impulse that comes after thirteen years; and every sinner — a spirit of folly enters him, and he is lacking the understanding that comes at forty years. Therefore it says: ״וְהָיָה אִם בֶּן״ — if we probe after the understanding that comes in the fortieth year, and he is considered as though he never reached the fortieth year — by this you shall know that he is fit to be flogged with a number that is not forty exactly but close to this number, for he is not a people of understanding."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:13:50.950618288Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}